<title>USA: US spot LPGs slightly weaker in quiet trade.</title>
<headline>US spot LPGs slightly weaker in quiet trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. spot liquefied petroleum gas prices were slightly weaker in dead trade on Wednesday amid weakening on NYMEX futures, players said.</p>
<p>Mont Belvieu propane was offered at 34.25 cents a gallon, while material in Conway sold for 35.125 cents, a quarter cent down from Tuesday.</p>
<p>Prices of normal butane were stable in both centers, with offers at 38.00 cents in Mont Belvieu and in Conway, players said.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1631</p>
